        "title": "Interesting place to visit",
        "text": "This is a good place to visit to view the temples and the process of Hindu cremation. We were here for almost 3 hours wandering around the site, and experiencing a cremation ceremony.  For the cremation a bit of respect is required for the family and friends, the best place is across the river, that way you are a respectful distance from the mourners, we checked with a few people and photos are ok as long as you are respectful. Take into account is that you will probably see the deceased during the cleansing of the body. What was unusual was the young guys going around selling candy floss. Definitely worth a visit, again a few local guides trying to get your business but this time we had a guide book which had a great map and explanations so we could go at our pace.",
