        "title": "Iconic place for Hindus to visit",
        "text": "This is by far the most amazing temple in Kathmandu. The temple is very sacred and holds utmost importance for Hindus. It is very clean and no photography is allowed.\n\nThere are many big and small temples of many gods and goddesses but you have main Shiv temple in the centre and other temples around it. The evening aarti at 7:00 PM on Bagmati river is special and it is one of its kind in Kathmandu. \n\nNear the river you will also find active crematorium and people getting cremated. So make sure that you pay respect and don't take photos.  \n\nYou should plan for at least 2-3 hours before starting your trip.",
