      {
        "review_id": 599074854,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r599074854-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "A distinctly different experience!",
        "text": "Pashupathinath is both a temple for prayer and a cremation site. It's a place where you can observe life thriving through the religious pujas, singing & dancing. At the same time death, loss and death rituals can be observed. It is a distinctly different perspective from the norm where rituals of life and death are segregated. Definitely worth visiting. The place is relatively easy to get to via public bus (which is what I took). \n\nDepending where you get off you'll have to navigate there. It is advisable to get there for the first puja of the evening which is said to be really auspicious. I somehow got pushed to the front so I got to see this puja. \n\nBe prepared to remove your shoes at the entrance and dress modestly.",
        "review_tip": null,
