      {
        "review_id": 598346741,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r598346741-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Amazing experience",
        "text": "You can spend whole day in Pashupatinath complex and not get bored! It's quite large area but easily accessible by foot (except of the central temple that can be entered only by Nepalese hindus), so walk around or sit down somewhere and just watch the life going on. The best spots are the banks of Bagmati River. You will be barely able to absorb all the things that are going on there, things that are unthinkable for Western minds but are perfectly normal for people from this part of Asia: hours long public cremations, kids fishing for valuables with magnet on the rope right underneath the cremations spots, people doing their daily hygiene in the dirty water of the sacred river, holy men (sadhus) with painted faces and dreadlocks... It might be culture shock for most of the people but is one of the most interesting places I have seen and it's definitely worth the visit.",
        "review_tip": null,
