      {
        "review_id": 598242622,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r598242622-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Kailash Manas Sarovar Yatra 24th June 2018",
        "text": "On the first day and the last day of our Kailash Manas sarovar tour, we visited the Pashupati nath temple to seek blessings.  The temple premises are clean and devoid of beggers and alm seeking people which we see in most of our temples.  The pooja conducted by 3-4 pandits was very religious an involve Rudram, Namkam etc.  People were asked to stand in the queue to have darshan of the Lord from any of the four dwaras (doors).  There were no short cuts or line breaking by the pilgrims.  During Aarti time in the evening, all the devotees are allowed to visit the Lord through every door in a line and mantra jal and flowers were given by the temple poojari at the end of Aarti.  Our experience was very divine in the temple premises and we felt like spending a lot of time there visiting several of the temples inside the premises.",
